-- title:
--   Zariski descent of isomorphisms of admissible rigidified formal mathcal O_D-modules
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a commutative ring $O$ with a ring homomorphism $\iota \colon W(\mathbb F_{p^2}) \to O$ (where `Zp2 p` is the ring of Witt vectors of `GaloisField p 2`), and a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $O/pO$, $pO$ being the ideal generated by $p$; here a `FormalODModule` over a ring is a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $F$ together with an action $a \mapsto \mathrm{act}(a)$ of `Zp2 p` and a series $\varpi$, all by endomorphisms of $F$, satisfying $\mathrm{act}(1) = \mathrm{id}$, multiplicativity and additivity of the action, $\varpi \circ \varpi = \mathrm{act}(p)$ and $\varpi \circ \mathrm{act}(a) = \mathrm{act}(\sigma a) \circ \varpi$ for the Witt vector Frobenius $\sigma$. Let $B$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, $\psi \colon O \to B$ a ring homomorphism, and assume $p$ is nilpotent in $B$. Let $t, t'$ be rigidified objects over $B$, each consisting of a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X$ over $B$, a natural number, and a pair of power series $\rho$ in two variables over $B/pB$, and assume both are admissible for $(\iota, \psi)$: the zero and one Lie parts of $X$ relative to the structure map built from $\iota$ and $\psi$ are complementary invertible $B$-modules, $X$ has height $4$, and $\rho$ is an isogeny of height $4$ times the given natural number from the reduction of $\Phi$ along $\psi$ to the reduction of $X$. Finally let $f \colon \mathrm{Fin}\, n \to B$ be a finite family generating the unit ideal, and suppose that for every $i$ the base changes of $t$ and $t'$ along $B \to B[1/f_i]$ (via `Localization.Away (f i)`) are isomorphic, where `IsIsomorphic` means: there are series $u, v$ and an $m \in \mathbb N$ with $u$ an $\mathcal O_D$-module homomorphism from the first module to the second, $v$ one in the opposite direction, $v \circ u$ and $u \circ v$ the identity, and the rigidifications matched in the sense that $\mathrm{act}(p^{m+n'}) \circ (\bar u \circ \rho) = \mathrm{act}(p^{m+n}) \circ \rho'$ on the reduction of the target, $\bar u$ being the reduction of $u$ modulo $p$. Then $t$ and $t'$ are isomorphic over $B$ in this same sense.
--
--   This is the gluing half of the assertion that isomorphism classes of admissible rigidified formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules form a Zariski sheaf, in the setting of Drinfeld's moduli description of $p$-adic uniformisation. It rests on the rigidity statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.eq_of_isODHom_of_act_pow_comp_map_comp_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.eq_of_isODHom_of_act_pow_comp_map_comp_eq) (uniqueness of a homomorphism compatible with the rigidifications) together with stability of admissibility under base change, [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.IsAdmissible.map_ringHom`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.IsAdmissible.map_ringHom), and is used in the construction of the moduli package and of the associated Zariski sheaf over Witt vector bases.
